window.EA_DATA={"items":[{"slug":"run","title":"Run","author":"Steve","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/d074f5a864.webp"},{"slug":"puzzling","title":"Puzzling","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5f74e351e5.webp"},{"slug":"lucky-charm","title":"Lucky Charm","author":"Bennie","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9c8b450059.webp"},{"slug":"hair","title":"Hair","author":"Janet","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3acd72e6f5.webp"},{"slug":"dichotomous","title":"Dichotomous","author":"Harry","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e309a1937d.webp"},{"slug":"colourful","title":"Colourful","author":"Sunny","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e3d2c57062.webp"},{"slug":"calmness","title":"Calmness","author":"Guija","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/27bab57970.webp"},{"slug":"blinded-by-the-dark","title":"Blinded By The Dark","author":"Yeonsoo","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/366aecf5c0.webp"},{"slug":"attention","title":"Attention","author":"Lune","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1f3837d513.webp"},{"slug":"20-years","title":"20 Years","author":"Steve","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5b8939bca2.webp"},{"slug":"childhood-friend","title":"Childhood Friend","author":"Albert","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/ba89a05310.webp"},{"slug":"clothes","title":"Clothes","author":"Hyungwon","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/33d8c23716.webp"},{"slug":"constant-attention","title":"Constant Attention","author":"Ara","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/69e70704b6.webp"},{"slug":"grandmas-tradition","title":"Grandma's Tradition","author":"Minchae","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/28acf4eb85.webp"},{"slug":"home-of-my-dream","title":"Home of My Dream","author":"Sian","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f57b8f6dae.webp"},{"slug":"korean-cat","title":"Korean Cat","author":"Jisu","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/06663e537c.webp"},{"slug":"lake","title":"Lake","author":"Lahee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/d0ec379e80.webp"},{"slug":"mountain-over-mountain","title":"Mountain Over Mountain","author":"Troy","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/ad335af4c9.webp"},{"slug":"petals","title":"Petals","author":"Lynn","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3e2ae92968.webp"},{"slug":"scenes-from-afar","title":"Scenes From Afar","author":"Serendipity","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/4f532f4909.webp"},{"slug":"the-remains","title":"The Remains","author":"Jinseon","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/8f96ac3d12.webp"},{"slug":"trees-of-hope","title":"Trees of Hope","author":"Brad","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2c1f63b3ed.webp"},{"slug":"under-the-ocean","title":"Under the Ocean","author":"Pat","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0d30b58d27.webp"},{"slug":"black-and-white","title":"Black and White","author":"Wonny","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0d27675343.webp"},{"slug":"her-eyes","title":"Her Eyes","author":"Jane","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/7086718254.webp"},{"slug":"kitten","title":"Kitten","author":"Teresa","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6f7152c028.webp"},{"slug":"my-persona","title":"My Persona","author":"Grace","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6686ae07db.webp"},{"slug":"night","title":"Night","author":"Yena","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/348483acbc.webp"},{"slug":"sad","title":"Sad","author":"Yura","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/8fb80704b0.webp"},{"slug":"sinking-flowers","title":"Sinking Flowers","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2ddc5838fa.webp"},{"slug":"wall-of-the-apartment","title":"Wall of the Apartment","author":"Kony","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/127d3d7998.webp"},{"slug":"rogue","title":"Rogue","author":"16 year old","meta":"","location":"","content":"I started to realize that we live in a society where artificial intelligence develops at a rate that we simply cannot follow, hence leading to questions such as if we are truly monitoring the thought process of A.I, and how humanity as a whole should react to the exponential growth of A. I's capabilities. By noticing how the dystopian societies depicted in media are disturbingly showing a close resemblance to today's society, it gave me the inspiration to draw the future scene from the science fiction film Terminator.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1b1b2a38dd.webp"},{"slug":"a-hundred-tears","title":"A Hundred Tears","author":"Stef","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/576eedffb4.webp"},{"slug":"ambivalence","title":"Ambivalence","author":"Amiaya","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/7e0ce2fbe3.webp"},{"slug":"yoga","title":"Yoga","author":"Grace","meta":"","location":"","content":"I drew the time when I was feeling tired, that I gave myself a new hobby of yoga.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3342a258bb.webp"},{"slug":"mental-surgery","title":"Mental Surgery","author":"Yunwoo Cha","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was struggling with increasing responsibilities in school and other parts of life. Sometimes, I wanted to give up and live as a disappointment. However, I still had a genuine desire to improve and achieve the successful future I want. Whenever I had thoughts of giving up, I wanted to cut out parts of myself that were causing those thoughts and only leave the rest that wanted success. The imagery of cutting myself reminded me of surgery. Thus, I decided to depict my mental situation as a person performing surgery on themself; a person that wants to rid themself of impurities.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/58c450be0b.webp"},{"slug":"beyond","title":"Beyond","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"As I transitioned from high school to university and experienced failure in the admissions process, I found myself in a situation where I had to take another step forward into society. During this time, I used the five traditional Korean colours and ink to express my inner self and convey my feelings of confusion. I wanted to express a situation that even I did not fully understand. This work portrays the confusing yet transcendent experience of my early twenties.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3aa2acec4e.webp"},{"slug":"bloom-of-recovery","title":"Bloom of Recovery","author":"Rebecca","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/7485e8d9fd.webp"},{"slug":"colours","title":"Colours","author":"Ian","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/22bd7a3c38.webp"},{"slug":"fear-of-the-future","title":"Fear of the Future","author":"Iryeong Cho","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c29fae1688.webp"},{"slug":"firework","title":"Firework","author":"Nina","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/466d01aa4c.webp"},{"slug":"happiness","title":"Happiness","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"During a period when I was struggling with the stress of university admissions, my friends and I tried to overcome our difficulties by making ourselves smile and laugh, even when it felt forced. While collecting photographs of people smiling, I came across an elderly man with an especially bright smile and decided to paint him.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1602642ec5.webp"},{"slug":"in-the-bloody-ocean","title":"In the Bloody Ocean","author":"Yunso","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/868b437f5c.webp"},{"slug":"jeju","title":"Jeju","author":"Kat","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/b36f0e3f90.webp"},{"slug":"mess","title":"Mess","author":"Bonny","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/39638014f9.webp"},{"slug":"poverty","title":"Poverty","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"After reading a book about poverty, I painted children on the other side of the world searching through rubbish. They live in the same world and at the same time as us, yet endure lives of hardship and deprivation that are completely different from ours. Who will understand them?\n\nI empathised with the helpless and exhausted child portrayed in the book and expressed that image through watercolour.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1015ffffb4.webp"},{"slug":"projection","title":"Projection","author":"Seohyun","meta":"","location":"","content":"This work reflects the artist’s identity through a pond where lotus flowers and goldfish exist in harmony. The fish is not simply an element of nature but a symbol of the artist herself, carrying personal significance because a fish appeared in her conception dream.\n\nThroughout the creative process, she gave considerable thought to the background. She repeatedly revised the colour and depth of the water, as these elements determined the overall atmosphere of the work. She felt the greatest happiness when she finally found a result with which she was satisfied. The process of studying and painting the lotus leaves, lotus flowers, and water was itself both meaningful and enjoyable.\n\nWhen she looks at the work now, she no longer sees it as merely a pond. It reminds her of her past self and the effort she made to complete it. Its central emotions extend beyond simple happiness or accomplishment. They include reflection and nostalgia for her past self, recovery gained through overcoming difficulties, and hope for her continued growth.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/208cbf3930.webp"},{"slug":"scenery","title":"Scenery","author":"Jeonga","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/97b638a21e.webp"},{"slug":"splendor","title":"Splendor","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"After reading books about women at the library, I began to reflect on the injustices within society and wanted to draw attention to women’s confidence and their position in society. In particular, I sought to represent the greatness of women through the dignified image of a Black woman surrounded by vibrant flowers.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/ffa6b5d82d.webp"},{"slug":"sunflower","title":"Sunflower","author":"Seoin","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/bb54bf69b6.webp"},{"slug":"sunrise","title":"Sunrise","author":"Jane","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e7e37e2219.webp"},{"slug":"tangled","title":"Tangled","author":"Moa","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c9d8e2b08f.webp"},{"slug":"teresas-prayer","title":"Teresa's Prayer","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"After the COVID-19 pandemic, the ways in which classes and schools operated changed completely, and I had to adapt to a rapidly changing society. This work is a prayer for everything undergoing change.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/a1b3385e17.webp"},{"slug":"an-autumn-evening","title":"An Autumn Evening","author":"Aiden","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was on a drive with my mom on an autumn evening. The sky was beautiful and I wanted to remember the scenery so I took a photo of it. I wish I was as beautiful as the sky I was seeing, and I wished someone else would think I am this beautiful and pleasing to watch.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/413cc848a8.webp"},{"slug":"an-awl","title":"An Awl","author":"Shay","meta":"","location":"","content":"During my vacation, which I spent studying for an exam, I constantly felt angry at myself because of how awful I was in the exam. I kept comparing myself to other people within the academy. It was the first time I genuinely started to doubt my abilities. I also questioned if I had a disorder which prevented me from getting good grades in the exam. I expressed my anger at the time by using paint drops that resemble the shape of an awl. An awl symbolizes how angry I was.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9338ec3c30.webp"},{"slug":"birds-eye","title":"Bird's Eye","author":"May","meta":"","location":"","content":"I achieved a big achievement in my academics by breaking through what I thought were my limits. I felt good and this moment reminded me of my dad's advice to persevere like a bird. This moment motivated me to create this drawing.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e9c1186f35.webp"},{"slug":"birthday-cake","title":"Birthday Cake","author":"Jine","meta":"","location":"","content":"This is a drawing of my birthday cake. I spent my birthday alone with my mom, without any friends. I felt a sense of loneliness. Barely anyone congratulated my birthday and I began to question myself: am I a bad friend? The fancy birthday cake contrasts with my lonely and hollow emotions I was feeling at the time.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2c2c065206.webp"},{"slug":"bloody","title":"Bloody","author":"Soyou","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was simply tired of everything. I was experiencing depression at this stage because of various reasons. Sometimes I would question if I really had depression because a frequently became frustrated at small things. I became more sensitive about everything my friend said. Traumatic memories recurred inside my brain. I was angry at myself because I couldn't control my emotions. My mind was just red, bloody and explosive.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/491581009a.webp"},{"slug":"cabin-light","title":"Cabin Light","author":"Ingrid","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/81ed879bd0.webp"},{"slug":"coloured-look","title":"Coloured Look","author":"Chiquita Evita Fatimah","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was looking too hard into a situation with a friend who was avoidant and unresponsive that it affected my mental health. To express myself, I wanted to paint a confronting gaze that symbolises the limbo of feelings using blue eyes to represent hints of sorrow and bold dominant red of anger.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e18be45d18.webp"},{"slug":"desert","title":"Desert","author":"Blair","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/a029bc308e.webp"},{"slug":"elg-i-vinterskogen","title":"Elg I Vinterskogen","author":"Rolf Andersen","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/43a8eaaff1.webp"},{"slug":"on-the-two-minutes-you-could-still-hear","title":"On the Two Minutes You Could Still Hear","author":"Alexis Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"I love you. I think\nI do. Because you're supposed to\nlove your family. Right?\n\nBut when I say I love you back, it goes down\nlike wet cement, scorches\nthe throat then hardens, slow and gray, towards the\ngut, where the guilt has set. The burn\nripples up. I feel nauseous.\n\nYou used to press a lollipop into my\npalm each time I came. That stopped\none day-not the way a storm stops violently,\nbut the way rain does:\npouring, drizzling, then only drops clinging to the leaves trickling\ndown, till the sun\nfinds and licks them dry.\n\nI'm sorry I only worried about you behind a screen.\nI'm sorry I couldn't-no, didn't-come to the white room, the white bed, the white gown.\nI'm sorry I lied every time you say you miss me, love me.\nI'm sorry I missed the funeral.\nI'm sorry I don't feel guilty.\n\nYesterday, I cried-the first time since the funeral.\nThe first since the sun parched my eyes.\nI read the letter your wife wrote you, 60 years sunk in the ink,\nher hand asking you to\nremember she loved you more. I iced my eyes so the swelling\nwouldn't show. The ice melted, dewed my lashes; my eyelids frozen, numb,\nas my saltwater mingled\nfor thirty minutes.\nBut for what? You? Her? Myself?\n\nI still have one lollipop somewhere, the last\none, gone soft and cloudy in its\nwrapper. I can't eat it. I keep meaning to throw it out. \nMaybe that's the closest thing to proof: that I kept\nthe sweetness\nlong after the sugar wept,\nlong after the wrinkled hand\nthat gave it was gone-\nand still can't make my fingers let go.\nI love you.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c26bc47daf.webp"},{"slug":"found-and-covered","title":"Found and Covered","author":"Marcus","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/b7ac81e4e0.webp"},{"slug":"fly-in-my-arms","title":"Fly In My Arms","author":"Yujoon","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was having a difficult time when I created this piece of artwork. I didn't want to go out; I stayed at home whenever possible. I didn't want to meet anyone because I was worried I would get hurt again. My self-esteem was lowest and I wished there was someone who would listen to me. I drew a butterfly because the emotion at the time reminded me how great it would be if someone could hug me like a butterfly.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/01caabc718.webp"},{"slug":"fractured-pieces","title":"Fractured Pieces","author":"Elena","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2a07e03d3f.webp"},{"slug":"memento-mori","title":"Memento Mori","author":"Dante","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9c625279e0.webp"},{"slug":"my-look","title":"My Look","author":"Judy","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was trying to hide from reality. Friends, family, people at school, people online. I hated one part of me that tried to be put on a facade when looked by other people. I thought there were two parts of me -- one with conscience and another with greed of being acknowledged.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/977105ec67.webp"},{"slug":"people-i-dont-know","title":"People I don't know","author":"Tiffany","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c615bb1641.webp"},{"slug":"pine-heart","title":"Pine Heart","author":"Yeonsu Oh","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/a8edfc0dc9.webp"},{"slug":"salt","title":"Salt","author":"Priya Nair","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f940b2128c.webp"},{"slug":"star-boy","title":"Star Boy","author":"Jiwon Seo","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/03d4e8d865.webp"},{"slug":"stardust-circuit","title":"Stardust Circuit","author":"Zara Kim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/976d0cf84c.webp"},{"slug":"system-error-404","title":"System Error 404","author":"Kai Tanaka","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e1212a66b5.webp"},{"slug":"tears","title":"Tears","author":"Pitch","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f066e049cc.webp"},{"slug":"universe","title":"Universe","author":"David","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6dcf65210c.webp"},{"slug":"water-carrier","title":"Water Carrier","author":"Amara Diallo","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/8336270572.webp"},{"slug":"white-hydrangea","title":"White Hydrangea","author":"Jay","meta":"","location":"","content":"I remember the time of the year when my grandparents visited our home. They always used to love the white flowers that bloomed along our village. Now I've realized that it has been so long since we have spent quality time together as a family. I miss those times and I wish I could go back to when I was young.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f242e36d64.webp"},{"slug":"i-dentity","title":"(I_)DENTITY","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this piece as a part of a university project. The concept of this piece stemmed from a loss of or confusion regarding one's identity, caused by having to take difficult decisions which in that point in time felt as if they would shape or define me. I combined a hanger hook and a teddy bear to create the piece, wherein the hook also resembles a question mark in a place where the head of the teddy bear should lie.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e8646a41ff.webp"},{"slug":"anxiety","title":"Anxiety","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"As my friends gradually began deciding on their future paths and university goals, I found myself becoming increasingly uncertain about my own.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5a09badd6a.webp"},{"slug":"blue","title":"Blue","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/b5202bbdd2.webp"},{"slug":"gaze","title":"Gaze","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"This artwork conveys a sense of quiet loneliness and emotional exhaustion. The character’s half-hidden face and distant gaze suggest someone who is withdrawn, carrying emotions that remain unspoken.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/684f6bee05.webp"},{"slug":"lonely","title":"Lonely","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"Although I continued to smile and interact with others as usual, there were moments when I felt an unexplained sense of emptiness.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0e51ed6d9b.webp"},{"slug":"psychedelic-remains","title":"Psychedelic Remains","author":"Bismah Saqib","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this piece whilst standing on the threshold between my academic and professional life, the point where I truly did not know what I was doing and where I would end up, so I did what I did best, which was making art. I used bright colors, nature and skulls because I wanted to integrate all that was around me in it's rawest form, but i wanted to keep it bright and colorful to exude a sense of whimsy and hope instead of making it melancholic or unsettling.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6d61485fca.webp"},{"slug":"quiet","title":"Quiet","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"This artwork reflects my experience of hiding my true thoughts and emotions within my friend group. Although I was surrounded by people, I often chose to stay silent because I was afraid that speaking honestly might create distance or misunderstandings.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/029a621ae2.webp"},{"slug":"self-reflection","title":"Self-Reflection","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"There is still a desire to be understood and to find hope.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/fb47c391d6.webp"},{"slug":"stress","title":"Stress","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"Despite being surrounded by friends and family, there are moments when it feels impossible to share what is truly on one's mind. The thick canopy hides the sky, creating a sense of suffocation and uncertainty about the future.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e0b2660459.webp"},{"slug":"uncertain-future","title":"Uncertain Future","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"As university applications, exams, and decisions about the future drew closer, I began to feel increasingly pressured by the need to have everything figured out.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e0b8dfd8f6.webp"},{"slug":"uncertain","title":"Uncertain","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"Everyone around me seemed to have clear goals and a sense of direction, while I felt as though I was still searching for mine.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/001f952bc2.webp"},{"slug":"waves","title":"Waves","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"The endless overlapping waves resemble the repetitive cycle of waking up, attending classes, studying, completing assignments, and preparing for exams.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c84dd94f5d.webp"},{"slug":"where-the-skin-sheds","title":"Where The Skin Sheds","author":"Saanvi Sinha","meta":"","location":"","content":"When I drew this piece, i was standing at a massive crossroad, facing the intense emotional friction of a drastic life  decision which was switching my future career from science to psychology.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f5e2c57296.webp"},{"slug":"a-sad-night","title":"A Sad Night","author":"Julie","meta":"","location":"","content":"This piece was inspired by the moment I learned that someone I deeply admired had achieved something I had worked toward for years. I congratulated them sincerely, but privately I was overwhelmed by envy and shame for feeling envious in the first place. I created this work while reflecting on how jealousy can feel explosive and uncontrollable despite being one of the emotions people are least willing to admit.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2cb6eda763.webp"},{"slug":"a-gentle-elsewhere","title":"A Gentle Elsewhere","author":"Yuki Tanabe","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/dfc9ea428f.webp"},{"slug":"angel-and-me","title":"Angel and Me","author":"Cielo","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this work after noticing how easily admiration can change the way someone behaves. I wanted to capture the unsettling transition between innocence and self-consciousness — the moment when being seen starts to matter more than simply being yourself.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/82bf4a81e2.webp"},{"slug":"beneath-the-silence","title":"Beneath the Silence","author":"Theo","meta":"","location":"","content":"This piece was inspired by the night after my grandfather’s funeral, when I watched my family sit together in silence without speaking about the grief. I remember feeling disturbed by how people could stand so close to each other emotionally yet still feel completely alone inside themselves.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/b586b41ab7.webp"},{"slug":"childhood","title":"Childhood","author":"Min","meta":"","location":"","content":"This piece was inspired by my childhood experience when I was scolded in school for crying.  I remember trying to hold back tears afterward because I became ashamed of appearing weak in front of others. The expression in this portrait reflects the moment innocence begins learning how to hide pain.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5063b2b312.webp"},{"slug":"eye-in-the-work","title":"Eye In The Work","author":"Seri","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/b1be7c6770.webp"},{"slug":"garden","title":"Garden","author":"Phoeny","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this work while going through a major change in my life. I had to abandon plans I had invested years into and accept that starting over was better than continuing down a path that no longer felt like my own.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/10d5937e22.webp"},{"slug":"growing-through-pain","title":"Growing Through Pain","author":"Lucky","meta":"","location":"","content":"My health was deteriorating and during those 3 months I realized what truly matters that is my parents and family ... Specially my mother was a ray of hope for me, resilience was found when I saw the times my health relapsed again and again and we had to go to hospitals it..it was then when I truly understood the power of mind and how sometimes positive thinking and social support work more than medicians..I drew this painting to remind myself of my minds endless potential and the ability to overcome anything just with belief.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2a9e6e558d.webp"},{"slug":"hold","title":"Hold","author":"Dara Olu","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/4cd3b94017.webp"},{"slug":"just-before-he-left","title":"Just Before He Left","author":"Noah","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this work while reflecting on how people remain in relationships long after emotional intimacy disappears. I wanted to capture the hollow stillness that exists when two people share the same space but are already emotionally elsewhere. I imagined the feeling of staying beside someone after realizing love has already ended, yet neither person has the courage to say it aloud.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/32d4763012.webp"},{"slug":"letting-it-collapse","title":"Letting It Collapse","author":"Lunes","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this work during a time when I felt physically and emotionally drained from pressure and burnout. Although people around me thought I was managing well, I felt detached from myself and wanted to express the feeling of quietly collapsing in a safe space. I also wanted someone to love me for just the way I am, not because of my academic achievements.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/10f42c0b76.webp"},{"slug":"my-childhood-world","title":"My Childhood World","author":"Milam","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this work while reflecting on childhood afternoons spent entertaining myself. I wanted to capture the strange freedom of building entire worlds from imagination, where toy pieces, animals, and fantasy could exist together without needing to make sense.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/2bbc6360f6.webp"},{"slug":"stiff-ache-tension-its-all-the-same-with-ptsd","title":"Stiff, Ache, Tension, Its All the Same with PTSD","author":"Angelina Waidelich","meta":"","location":"","content":"My situation was that I was dealing my PTSD and how it physically manifests In my body besides my depression and anxiety. Such as anger through stomping, picking at my skin, feeling tightness in my throat and ankle, and my body being exhausted in general. As well as how my emotions manifest too.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0e7a32b7ef.webp"},{"slug":"stitched-silence","title":"Stitched Silence","author":"Lavender","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this art piece to express my heartbreak during a time when I had completely lost myself. My self-esteem was at its lowest, and I couldn’t even see myself as who I really was. That’s why I portrayed myself as a boy instead of a girl, it reflects how disconnected I felt from my own identity. This drawing carries my frustration, anger, and the emotions I couldn’t put into words at that time.\n\nOne of his eyes is covered, symbolizing shame, while the other holds a faint hint of water, even though he isn’t crying. It represents pain that hasn’t fully escaped yet. The small scratch near his eye shows how blind he was to the betrayal right in front of him. On one hand, he wears a watch to show how much time he wasted on a single person, time that can never be recovered. In his other hand, there is an axe, representing the anger that kept building inside him.\n\nThe stitches on his neck symbolize the loss of words caused by heartbreak, the feeling of being unable to speak, explain, or express the pain he was carrying. The lines on his arm reflect the harm he inflicted on himself while trying to cope with overwhelming stress. Giving him a monster-like form beneath a human exterior shows how unreal, broken, and disconnected he felt inside. The slight smile on his face represents silent pain, the kind that exists even when you don’t fully realize how deeply you’re hurting.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f62e7a21be.webp"},{"slug":"the-last-autumn-before-we-grew-up","title":"The Last Autumn Before We Grew Up","author":"Eli","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this work while thinking about how childhood memories can feel warm and lonely at the same time. Although in my artwork, the scene looks peaceful, I also wanted to capture the hollow feeling that childhood does not last forever. I created this piece when I was 10 years old and it was Halloween. I sat outside with my cousin after a family argument and pretended everything was normal. At the time, I wished to myself my childhood wouldn't be over.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1a548d0157.webp"},{"slug":"to-fly-and-fall","title":"To Fly and Fall","author":"Neeva","meta":"","location":"","content":"When I created this piece it was after summer break when I had spent good times with my friends at the time. Once school started however these some of these friends started excluding me from plans and this made me confused because I hadn’t done anything hurtful to them. But I later realized this was a good thing because I realized I didn’t really like the people they changed into so not being friends with them was better and I knew I had other good friends to support me. I also knew I would always have the good memories I made with them. This piece represents these emotions by illustrating the story of Icarus who had a good time flying but got too close to the sun and fell but as he fell he was happy that he was able to fly at least.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/ea905e6af4.webp"},{"slug":"weight-of-ochre","title":"Weight of Ochre","author":"Maya Ostroff","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e654c596e6.webp"},{"slug":"what-remains","title":"What Remains","author":"Simone Albrecht","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/7cfe1e7372.webp"},{"slug":"who-are-you","title":"Who Are You","author":"Jinho Kwon","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5b8dd73b6e.webp"},{"slug":"the-inner-flame","title":"The Inner Flame","author":"Minjae Jeong","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1145a4bc6a.webp"},{"slug":"under-the-moonlight","title":"Under the Moonlight","author":"Seoyeon Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/376c3da5f6.webp"},{"slug":"encounter","title":"Encounter","author":"Junhyuk Park","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6ba2861964.webp"},{"slug":"empty-branches","title":"Empty Branches","author":"Yujin Choi","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/61a3cb59b6.webp"},{"slug":"by-the-window","title":"By the Window","author":"Nayoon Kim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/dd86fa0358.webp"},{"slug":"loss","title":"Loss","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was in a situation where I had to end a friendship. I didn't feel sad, nor did I feel happy, but it felt as though a corner of my heart had been left completely empty.\n\nIt feels like nothing is left.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f955590729.webp"},{"slug":"vigilance","title":"Vigilance","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"It was a time when I had to make a new start among strangers. On the outside, I pretended to be calm, but on the inside, I was constantly worried about making a mistake, reacting sensitively to the looks and the atmosphere around me. I wanted to project my own state of mind at that time through the image of a crouching tiger.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/bd20257bf8.webp"},{"slug":"birds","title":"Birds","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"I created this artwork during a time when I had lost my confidence after failing to achieve the results I expected. Although it felt as though everything had come to a standstill, I was able to gradually stand back up as small challenges and new experiences built up. The flowers filling the peacock symbolize the learning and growth gained throughout that process.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9ebc9b8824.webp"},{"slug":"reversal","title":"Reversal","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"When I transferred schools during middle school to prepare for admission to an arts high school, I was unable to achieve the top grades I had expected and remained in the upper-middle range. This work expresses a garden of the mind in which everything has been turned upside down, capturing the confusion and anxiety I experienced while questioning whether art was truly the right path for me.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/97eb71cd6b.webp"},{"slug":"youth","title":"Youth","author":"Nyang","meta":"","location":"","content":"A different kind of happiness only felt back then","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/57c9a7ad3f.webp"},{"slug":"angel-and-strawberry","title":"Angel and Strawberry","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"Under the theme “Things I Love,” I painted a fountain where strawberries grow instead of flowers, using my favourite fruit, strawberries, and angels, which fascinated me at the time, as the central motifs.\n\nAlthough I had to complete the work quickly because of a deadline, it is a painting that I would like to hang in my room when I eventually live on my own. I enjoyed creating it because I filled it with the things I love. However, when I look at it for a long time, it can also leave me with a subtle sense of emptiness.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/106e4f8035.webp"},{"slug":"me","title":"Me","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"This work represents a period when I could see only my flaws. I felt that everything about me, including my appearance and personality, was inadequate, causing me to lose confidence and withdraw into myself.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/debdc07d42.webp"},{"slug":"the-dawn-left-behind","title":"The Dawn Left Behind","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"This work depicts a place filled with memories of my father. He moved to another region for work, and I would occasionally visit his home. Those moments were precious because they were time shared entirely between my father and me.\n\nI would often wake early in the morning to the rustling sounds of my father preparing to leave for work. After he left, I would remain alone in bed, turning from side to side and looking up at the sky. It was an in-between time when the darkness of night had not completely disappeared and the brightness of morning had not yet fully emerged. The sky at that hour had an ambiguous colour formed by many different shades blending together.\n\nEven the uneventful hours spent waiting for my father to return were precious to me. However, circumstances have changed, and I can no longer experience those moments. Even if I want to return to them, all I can do is miss them.\n\nThe uncertain colours of the sky seemed to reflect the complexity of my emotions. The emptiness and longing I feel now are bittersweet.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9e345f4cc5.webp"},{"slug":"one-day","title":"One Day","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"It was a day I almost ran late. In contrast to the chilly air, the sunlight pouring down from the sky was intense—so intense that the world looked a bit washed out in white. Gasping for breath, I was running with all my might, and the moment I entered the market, a bright light enveloped me as if to blind me. I froze when I saw the light piercing through the crowds of people. That strong yet radiant sunlight felt as though it was comforting me. In the midst of the difficult situation I was facing at the time, it felt like it was embracing me—confused and filled with self-blame—more warmly than anyone else could. From this warmth, I found hope that someday, I would be able to recover from the pain.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/94a4acda2d.webp"},{"slug":"the-recurring-dawn","title":"The Recurring Dawn","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"I was living in circumstances that I had not chosen, surrounded by unwanted concerns and endless thoughts. I would move through my daily routine as usual, but whenever dawn arrived, feelings of depression would rise within me. When I lay alone in bed and stared at the ceiling, the thoughts I had tried so hard to avoid would rush over me like a wave. As the saying goes, depression is water-soluble: once you begin to get wet, it quickly consumes you.\n\nAs I remained awake and lost in thought, things that had previously been invisible gradually came into view—the dust floating in the air, clothes scattered untidily around the room, and other minor details of everyday life. They seemed to reflect who I was. The residue of my emotions drifted through my mind, while unorganised thoughts accumulated everywhere.\n\nOnce again, I face the recurring dawn alone.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/46539669da.webp"},{"slug":"blooming-flower","title":"Blooming Flower","author":"Kyung Chung","meta":"","location":"","content":"This work depicts a moment during a university retreat when I was looking at the sea alone. At the time, I was not accustomed to being by myself and felt lonely. However, as I gazed at the sea, my thoughts and emotions gradually became calmer.\n\nAfter this experience, I began to realise that spending time alone might not necessarily be a negative thing, and I was able to let go of my fear of being alone.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/a4dc5d295f.webp"},{"slug":"is-it-over","title":"Is It Over?","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/01e96bc1e2.webp"},{"slug":"jeju-in-wraps","title":"Jeju In Wraps","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c093bfd0a3.webp"},{"slug":"pandemic-outbreak","title":"Pandemic Outbreak","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0d1a6ffc24.webp"},{"slug":"priced-differently","title":"Priced Differently","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/c9403b3fec.webp"},{"slug":"raised-in-ruin","title":"Raised In Ruin","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/375421aecd.webp"},{"slug":"tiger-in-my-dream","title":"Tiger In My Dream","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e72c15156b.webp"},{"slug":"watcher","title":"Watcher","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/e91ff7dce3.webp"},{"slug":"who-gets-chosen","title":"Who Gets Chosen","author":"Anonymous","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3049132a80.webp"},{"slug":"global","title":"Global","author":"Dongwon Hwang","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/add1d229e1.webp"},{"slug":"hell-poverty","title":"Hell = Poverty","author":"Jeonghyun Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/62eeb2d175.webp"},{"slug":"past-present-and-future","title":"Past, Present, and Future","author":"Jian Suh","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1b38758639.webp"},{"slug":"imbalance-of-food","title":"Imbalance of Food","author":"Jian Suh","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3f36140e38.webp"},{"slug":"life-under-water","title":"Life Under Water","author":"Jian Suh","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/7882d1e19f.webp"},{"slug":"child-marriage-is-a-prison","title":"Child Marriage is a Prison","author":"Jian Suh","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/d9582baa64.webp"},{"slug":"shattered-identity-the-defectors-cry","title":"Shattered Identity: The Defector's Cry","author":"Jihu Park","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/29648a335a.webp"},{"slug":"good-health-bad-health","title":"Good Health, Bad Health","author":"Luke Hwang","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/b282b37c83.webp"},{"slug":"the-unseen-in-society","title":"The Unseen in Society","author":"Luke Hwang","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/4f7108dfc6.webp"},{"slug":"fragile","title":"Fragile","author":"Rachel Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6a81ae8ae0.webp"},{"slug":"untitled","title":"Untitled","author":"Seohyun Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/4a73f96572.webp"},{"slug":"collapse-of-the-city","title":"Collapse of the City","author":"Seunghwan Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1d3674c5ae.webp"},{"slug":"us","title":"Us","author":"Suhyun Kim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/cd5ff08081.webp"},{"slug":"red-tide","title":"Red Tide","author":"Suhyun Kim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5ec509642e.webp"},{"slug":"a-lonely-fish","title":"A Lonely Fish","author":"Yena An","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/117adecc3a.webp"},{"slug":"dual-nature-of-water","title":"Dual Nature of Water","author":"Yeonjun Im","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/24453ee142.webp"},{"slug":"my-reliable-self","title":"My Reliable Self","author":"Ok-soon Oh","meta":"F | 77 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Donam-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father was sentenced to seven years in prison, incarcerated at Daejeon Prison, and subsequently executed by firing squad; she only came to learn this truth when she turned 20 years old. Her widowed mother endured extreme hardships, farming completely on her own to raise both her and a half-sibling who was seven years younger.\n\nThrough her artwork, she primarily expressed her deep longing for her father and her profound sorrow for her mother's lifelong sacrifices.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/d6918a5f66.webp"},{"slug":"flowers-and-butterflies","title":"Flowers and Butterflies","author":"Yeon-ok Hyun","meta":"F | 83 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Odeung-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father was dragged away by a police officer, imprisoned in Daegu Prison, and subsequently went missing. She was five years old at the time and the second of three daughters. She was raised by her widowed mother, and with her mother's devotion, all three sisters were able to graduate from elementary school. Although they endured many hardships, she recalled and expressed her deep longing for the pure, warm days of her childhood and her profound gratitude for her mother.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/278238c79e.webp"},{"slug":"a-peaceful-mind","title":"A Peaceful Mind","author":"Yeon-sook Ko","meta":"F | 78 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Nohyeong-dong, Jeju-si","content":"She shared that long after the events, she learned that her grandfather had been stabbed with a bamboo spear during the April 3 Incident and was brought back home, where he eventually passed away despite the family's care. Born as the eldest of seven children into a deeply impoverished household, she had to drop out of elementary school and spent most of her childhood looking after her younger siblings. Reflecting on a lifetime of facing poverty and endless hardships, she expressed her deep yearning to finally find a peaceful mind through this artwork.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/587b463ca6.webp"},{"slug":"tree-of-hope","title":"Tree of Hope","author":"Soon-ye Kim","meta":"F | 76 years old | Daughter-in-law of 4·3 Incident Victim","location":"Bonggae-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father-in-law was killed in Myeongdoam.\n\nHer mother-in-law had never spoken of it, so she was completely unaware of this fact until she discovered it during the process of registering as a bereaved family member.\n\nHaving faced multiple personal and family hardships over the past few years, she had been under immense stress; however, through this artwork, she expressed her present journey of healing as she participates in the center's programs.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/a532bac951.webp"},{"slug":"a-pretty-rabbit-garden","title":"A Pretty Rabbit Garden","author":"Kyung-ja Kim","meta":"F | 84 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Ora-dong, Jeju-si","content":"She was seven years old during the April 3 Incident when her father was captured by the military and police on his way to his wife's family home; he was imprisoned in Masan, South Gyeongsang Province, and subsequently went missing. According to what she heard from her mother about the situation at the time, the police came to their house to arrest them, forcing them to flee and seek refuge in Minorium and Mount Halla. Although she felt uncomfortable expressing her life history through spoken language, she conveyed that she is finding great emotional comfort and solace through creating her artwork in the art therapy program.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5e8049558d.webp"},{"slug":"ive-lived-well-until-now-lets-be-happy-from-now-on","title":"I've Lived Well Until Now, Let's Be Happy From Now On","author":"Chun-saeng Lee","meta":"F | 79 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Geumak-ri, Hallim-eup, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, armed guerrillas slaughtered and ate a pig raised by her grandmother; because of this, her father was mistaken for being part of the same guerrilla group and was subsequently executed by firing squad by the counter-insurgency forces. Following her father's death, her mother remarried, and her older sisters left for the mainland to earn money, leaving her to be raised solely by her grandparents in a grandparent-headed household. Though her childhood was fraught with hardship from poverty and isolation, she expressed a warm sense of \"hope\" for her remaining days through this artwork.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9b7787fff5.webp"},{"slug":"the-sound-of-bells-in-my-heart","title":"The Sound of Bells in My Heart","author":"In-seon Kim","meta":"F | 85 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Donam-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her second older brother was killed. She was nine years old at the time and the youngest among three sons and two daughters. Having always strived to live with a bright and positive mindset, she expressed through this artwork her core philosophy of living each day with a sense of a fresh, brand-new beginning.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/13af76a116.webp"},{"slug":"the-sound-of-bells-in-my-heart-geum-saeng-shin","title":"The Sound of Bells in My Heart","author":"Geum-saeng Shin","meta":"F | 80 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Yeongpyeong-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father was killed by firing squad at Teojinmok in Seongsan, Seogwipo. Because she was so young at the time, she has no memory of her father's face, but she grew up hearing about him through her mother. Reflecting on her difficult life story—having lost her spouse at an early age and raising her children entirely on her own—she expressed her deep hope that her remaining days will be peaceful and filled with good health.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/6ca21ce4ab.webp"},{"slug":"my-tree-of-hope","title":"My Tree of Hope","author":"Ae-ja Oh","meta":"F | 83 years old | Daughter-in-law of 4·3 Incident Victim","location":"Yeongpyeong-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father-in-law was killed, leaving her mother-in-law to raise her husband and sister-in-law alone. After marrying through a matchmaker, she lived with and cared for both her mother-in-law and grandmother-in-law while managing a dry-field farm and an orchard. Looking back on those challenging times when resources were scarce, she reflected on how they endured by placing the utmost importance on family harmony, and she expressed that this artwork represents a tree of hope symbolizing health, freedom, and new challenges.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/89700dfd77.webp"},{"slug":"ill-give-you-an-old-house-give-me-a-new-house","title":"I'll Give You an Old House, Give Me a New House","author":"Young-soon Heo","meta":"F | 78 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Yongdam-dong, Jeju-si","content":"Her biological father was killed during the April 3 Incident. She experienced severe emotional distress due to deep depression, but her condition has been gradually improving as she participates in the center's programs and builds friendships with fellow participants. She expressed that creating this artwork brought back warm and comforting memories of her childhood, recalling the joyful times she spent playing in the sand by the seashore when she was young.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3335d8264f.webp"},{"slug":"looking-back-at-the-past-thinking-of-tomorrow","title":"Looking Back at the Past, Thinking of Tomorrow","author":"Han-yong Kim","meta":"M | 80 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Donghong-dong, Seogwipo-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, his biological father, biological grandfather, adoptive father, and adoptive grandfather were all killed.\n\nHis biological father was taken to Incheon Prison and went missing. Both his biological and adoptive grandfathers were executed by firing squad at their homes. After retiring from his career as a researcher and entering his twilight years, he has recently had many worries regarding health issues. However, comparing his current life to his lonely and isolated past, he expressed contentment and deep gratitude for the stable, peaceful life he now enjoys, surrounded by a large family.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f426b9e0f1.webp"},{"slug":"from-loneliness-to-peace-and-hope","title":"From Loneliness to Peace and Hope","author":"Yoon-ji Kim","meta":"F | 78 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Ildo 2-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her biological father, who was an elementary school teacher, was killed. She was only a week old at the time, and following her mother's remarriage, she grew up moving between relatives' homes. Having spent much of her childhood isolated and alone, she lived with a frequent sense of loneliness throughout her life. However, she expressed that her children, with whom she shares a close and loving relationship, now live nearby, and she feels deeply grateful for her current life, which has become much better than before.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/1334e7dc5c.webp"},{"slug":"a-sorrowful-past-a-happy-present","title":"A Sorrowful Past, A Happy Present","author":"Eul-saeng Hong","meta":"F | 91 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Daeheul-ri, Jocheon-eup, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her biological father was dragged away by the police while farming and was subsequently executed by firing squad. She was ten years old at the time and recalled having to hide in the Gotjawal forest with her family to escape the police who threatened them at gunpoint, enduring severe hunger. She also explained how hopeless their situation became after their house and fields were entirely burned down. Compared to those dark times, she expressed deep gratitude for her current life, which has now become stable and secure.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/3d3c0b67d1.webp"},{"slug":"mother-worked-until-the-moon-rose","title":"Mother Worked Until the Moon Rose","author":"Mu-ok Park","meta":"F | 78 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Dodu-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her biological father was killed when she was only three months old. She shared how heartbreaking it was to witness her biological mother working relentlessly to support the family while going to the prison every single day in a desperate attempt to save her husband's life. This artwork captures her deep pity, longing, and gratitude for her mother, who did nothing but suffer throughout her entire life before passing away.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9bd996fa75.webp"},{"slug":"memories-of-april-3-and-healing","title":"Memories of April 3, and Healing","author":"Cheol-bu Moon","meta":"M | 89 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Sehwa-ri, Gujwa-eup, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, his biological mother and older brother were killed. He shared that he vividly remembers the exact circumstances of their deaths, and he retains a distinct memory of every terrifying, near-death experience he faced when he was summoned to the police station. He expressed that participating in the art therapy program feels like being liberated from all of his burdens, proving to be a truly profound experience for him.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/81260c6a1d.webp"},{"slug":"sorrow-and-joy","title":"Sorrow and Joy","author":"Bok-ja Ko","meta":"F | 74 years old | Daughter-in-law of 4·3 Incident Victim","location":"Dodu-dong, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father-in-law was executed by firing squad in Dodu. She spoke of the hardships she endured as she took full responsibility for the household finances while nursing her spouse, who had suffered from lifetime trauma before battling cancer. Through this artwork, she expressed her gratitude for the immense psychological comfort and solace she has found by participating in the art therapy program.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/420e95df02.webp"},{"slug":"my-heartbreaking-father","title":"My Heartbreaking Father","author":"Soon-haeng Oh","meta":"F | 82 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Samyang-dong, Jeju-si","content":"Her biological father was killed during the April 3 Incident. Her father-in-law was also imprisoned at Mokpo Prison during the incident and was subsequently executed by firing squad. Although her life following the tragedy was a continuous cycle of poverty and hardship, she has always made an effort to live joyfully. This artwork captures and expresses her deep, tender longing for her biological father.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/09a1f556f7.webp"},{"slug":"the-naked-log-deer","title":"The Naked Log Deer","author":"Young-ja Lee","meta":"F | 80 years old | Daughter-in-law of 4·3 Incident Victim","location":"Donam-dong, Jeju-si","content":"She heard that during the April 3 Incident, her father-in-law was 23 years old when he went missing. Her husband was only 7 years old at the time and grew up as an only child under a single mother. Her mother-in-law never remarried, scraping by to raise her son on her own. Although marrying into a family with so much deep-seated pain made her journey difficult, she expressed that her current life feels joyful, thanks to participating in the center's art therapy program.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/5a60eace77.webp"},{"slug":"seeing-the-persimmon-tree-brings-me-joy","title":"Seeing the Persimmon Tree Brings Me Joy","author":"Bok-ja Ko","meta":"F | 79 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Daeheul-ri, Jocheon-eup, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her father, who was the second of seven siblings, was killed alongside two of his brothers while moving from one cave to another in search of refuge. Following this tragedy, her grandfather also passed away from a broken heart. Due to past trauma combined with recent losses over the past few years—including the passing of her spouse and other close family members—she carried a profound sense of grief and deep mourning. However, she expressed through this artwork that she feels herself gradually healing through the art therapy program.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/68220cdc3b.webp"},{"slug":"the-kitchen-hearth","title":"The Kitchen Hearth","author":"Jung-ja Oh","meta":"F | 77 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Nohyeong-dong, Jeju-si","content":"Her father was killed during the April 3 Incident. She recalls her childhood, which was plagued by poverty, and how her eyes and nose would run from the thick smoke whenever she lit a fire in the hearth to cook rice. She lost her spouse at an early age and spent her youth working relentlessly as the sole breadwinner of the household. However, she expressed that her current life is happy, as she now spends her days doing volunteer work and participating in healing programs at the center.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/9f1c7ee440.webp"},{"slug":"it-was-so-heartbreaking","title":"It Was So Heartbreaking","author":"Young-soo Byun","meta":"F | 81 years old | Bereaved Families of the 4·3 Incident","location":"Yusuam-ri, Aewol-eup, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her biological father, who was an elementary school teacher, went missing, and her biological mother was killed by unidentified assailants. Her youngest sibling also passed away due to a lack of care, leaving only her older brother and herself to move from one relative's house to another, enduring a deeply painful childhood. This artwork seeks to reflect and express the profound grief and sadness she experienced at the time of her mother's tragic loss.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/ed77b7f546.webp"},{"slug":"the-long-journey-of-my-life","title":"The Long Journey of My Life","author":"Jeong-hee Lee","meta":"F | 85 years old | 4·3 Incident Survivor","location":"Sineom-ri, Aewol-eup, Jeju-si","content":"During the April 3 Incident, her biological mother was killed, and after her biological father remarried, she moved up to the mainland. She herself was left with a scar on the back of her neck from a bamboo spear attack by the armed rebels. Finding it too painful to face those agonizing memories, she was unable to set foot in her hometown for 65 years. Instead, she built a self-made life on the mainland, working with a sewing machine to make clothes and run her own business. Even now, she finds it difficult to bring back those memories because recalling that time is simply too horrific. This artwork expresses the deep regrets and reflections of a life lived intensely, overcoming immense hardship.","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0b88e537ac.webp"},{"slug":"consumption","title":"Consumption","author":"Boksoon Yoo","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/81d0770c98.webp"},{"slug":"simple-joy","title":"Simple Joy","author":"Changnyeo Jo","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/ae6c90e1bf.webp"},{"slug":"my-fruits","title":"My Fruits","author":"Cheolgyu Kim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/4488f22089.webp"},{"slug":"sequence-of-organics","title":"Sequence of Organics","author":"Chunrye Han","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/77f6ad2f23.webp"},{"slug":"sliced","title":"Sliced","author":"Deoksoo Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/77c8f0e744.webp"},{"slug":"self","title":"Self","author":"Giboon Kim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/72b8024ed9.webp"},{"slug":"whole-watermelon","title":"Whole Watermelon","author":"Heeson Kang","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/444e17cbf7.webp"},{"slug":"flower","title":"Flower","author":"Hwanoh Jeong","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/61a8d13864.webp"},{"slug":"still-growing","title":"Still Growing","author":"Insook Lee","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/83a24fa4e0.webp"},{"slug":"plant-study","title":"Plant Study","author":"Okmae Lim","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/53161a3c16.webp"},{"slug":"trying-to-fix","title":"Trying To Fix","author":"Sangok Jeong","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/79337e8a0a.webp"},{"slug":"dream-flower","title":"Dream Flower","author":"Seongnam Park","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/f37864c5f5.webp"},{"slug":"bloom-in-heat","title":"Bloom In Heat","author":"Youngsoo Kwon","meta":"","location":"","content":"","info":"","qa":"","img":"assets/archive/0241cabe80.webp"}],"reports":[{"slug":"art-emotion-and-metadata-a-study-of-emotional-expression-acr","title":"Art, Emotion, and Metadata: A Study of Emotional Expression Across Age Groups","desc":"Using 64 Google Form responses collected in Korean and English from May to July 2026, the study found that negative emotions were more common than positive ones, with emptiness, hope, recovery, and loneliness appearing most frequently.","thumb":"assets/reports/0488c3de17.webp","url":"https://zenodo.org/records/21699819","blocks":[]},{"slug":"how-art-can-help-cure-depression","title":"How Art Can Help Cure Depression","desc":"Depression and anxiety rates in youth increased sharply, causes involving increased uses of social media and smartphones...","thumb":"assets/reports/ed789cd853.webp","url":"","blocks":[{"c":"[b][size=6]Depression ➔\n+20% in the past year[/size][/b]\n\nDepression and anxiety rates in youth increased sharply, causes involving increased uses of social media and smartphones.","img":"assets/reports/7ffaf7d4ce.webp"},{"c":"[b][size=5]What depression may feel like[/size][/b]\n\nDepression in young adults often feels like an overwhelming mix of intense irritability, persistent numbness, deep exhaustion, and worthlessness, rather than just sadness. It causes significant withdrawal from friends, a loss of passion for hobbies, poor concentration, and drastic changes in sleep and appetite.\n\nYoung adults face high rates of depression due to a combination of intense academic/occupational pressure, social media comparison, financial stress (like student loans), and major life transitions, \nsuch as starting careers or relationships","img":"assets/reports/person.svg"},{"c":"[right][b][size=5]How can we help?[/size][/b][/right]\n\nTeenagers experiencing depression should first talk to a trusted adult—like a parent, teacher, or counselor—and seek professional help, such as therapy (CBT/IPT) or medical advice. Daily coping strategies include staying active, maintaining a regular sleep schedule, healthy eating, and connecting with friends.\n\nFocus on achievable daily tasks (e.g., taking a shower, walking outside) to build momentum. Reduce screen time or take breaks from social media to avoid negative comparisons or stress.","img":""},{"c":"[b][size=5]‘Post-traumatic stress disorder’[/size][/b]\n\nAround 70% of people globally experience a potentially traumatic event in their lifetime, with over 3.9% experiencing Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder (PTSD). \n\nRecent data indicates rising trends in trauma exposure, particularly among females (37.4% in 2023/4) and growing rates of PTSD, which increased from 3.4% to 7.5% in some studies (WHO).","img":"assets/reports/54edd7602d.webp"},{"c":"[right][b][size=5]How art may help cure[/size][/b][/right]\n\nArt helps resolve trauma because it is a non-verbal medium to process memories without having to express them through language. Using visual arts, photography or other creative mediums allows individuals to externalize, visualize, and manage overwhelming feelings in a safe, controlled way, fostering emotional regulation and reducing symptoms of PTSD, anxiety, and depression. \n\nActively creating art activates the brain's medial prefrontal cortex and amygdala, enhancing emotional regulation and improving cognitive processing of trauma.","img":"assets/reports/d44e0f9e83.webp"},{"c":"[b][size=5]The science of trauma[/size][/b]\n\nTrauma, particularly in childhood, can shrink the hippocampus (responsible for memory) and increase the reactivity of the amygdala. The brain becomes oversensitive to threats, causing constant vigilance, flashbacks, or emotional numbness. Trauma is not just a cognitive memory; it is stored in the body, manifesting as chronic pain, fatigue, and tension.  Trauma involves a hyperactive amygdala (threat detector), a diminished prefrontal cortex (rational thought), and a reduced hippocampus (memory), leading to lasting emotional and physiological dysregulation.","img":""}]}]};